  "body": "## Summary\n\n- remove the queued-request `AsyncResource` implementation and regression test previously added on this branch\n- document that this fork does not support async-context propagation\n- direct callers to carry request-scoped state explicitly outside the transport\n\nThe net code diff against `master` is empty; this PR now adds documentation only.\n\n## Context\n\n[nodejs/undici#5982](https://github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5982) preserves `AsyncLocalStorage` state for queued requests by adding `node:async_hooks` integration. This fork intentionally does not support async context, `AsyncResource`, `AsyncLocalStorage`, or other `async_hooks` behavior, so that upstream change is not being adopted.\n\nA source audit of `nxtedition/undici` and `nxtedition/nxt-undici`, including the scheduler and trace dependencies used by `nxt-undici`, found no existing runtime use to remove outside the implementation previously introduced by this PR.\n\n## Validation\n\n- unit suite: 790 passed, 2 skipped\n- node-test suite: 156 passed\n- TypeScript declarations: passed\n- ESLint: passed\n- `git diff --check`: passed\n\nValidated with Node.js 26.7.0 on commit `8e187cc1ebc5ca52b8f5bcb6101929e7f2e842ea`.\n",
